        <p>ST. JOHN'S PRESBYTERIAN CHURCH. WILDERSPOOL CAUSEWAY. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), JANUARY 24, 1915. Preacher: Rev. W. REID. 10.45 a.m.: "Little by Little." 6.30 p.m.: "Crossing the Sea." Seat, Book, and Hearty Welcnme for Strangers.</p>
        <p>13ADGATE WESLEYAN CHURCH.—WesIey Guild. Thursday, Jan. 28th, Sermon at 4 p.m. Rev. J. E. RATTENBURY. Lecture at 7.30 p.m. Subject: "The War and the Churches." Chair- man, Joseph Bailey, Esq., J.P. Collection at each Service for the Guild Funds. Tea in the Guild Room at 5.30 p.m., Sixpence each. All are heartily invited.</p>
        <p>CAIRO-STREET CHAPEL. WARRINGTON. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY). JANUARY 24. Preacher: Rev. IRVINE LISTER. 10.30 a.m.: "The Church Without Walls." 8.30 p.m.: "Abraham Lincoln's Motto." All Made Welcome.</p>
        <p>LATCHFORD BAPTIST CHURCH SUNDAY, JANUARY 24th. 1916. Preacher: Mr. E. LLOYD JONES. Morning, 10.30. Evening, 6. All Welcome. Hymn Books Provided.</p>
        <p>C- HRISTADELPHIAN MEETING ROOM, BOLD-STREET, WARRINGTON. Free Bible Address SUNDAY NEXT. at 6.30 p.m. Subject: "That old Serpent, the Devil and Satan." Mr. B. LAKE, Manchester. PRIMITIVE METHODIST CHURCH, LEGH-STREET, WARRINGTON. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), JANUARY 24, 1915. Morning, 10.30: Rev. A. J. CHESSUM. Evening, 6.30: Mr. B. T. PARKES.</p>
        <p>CIOLBORNE-STREET BAPTIST CHURCH, "u WARRINGTON. TO-MORROW (Sunday), JAN. 24th. Morning. 10.45: Evening, 6.30. Mr. A. E. HOYLE, B.A.—THURSDAY, 7.45 p.m.: Young People's Guild. Speaker, Mr. W. ROWLAND. Subject: "Peace Terms. What?"</p>
