        <p>RUNCORN UNION. COOK REQUIRED. Required at the Workhouse, Dutton, near Warrington, a Female to undertake the duties of Cook. Salary, £25 per annum, with board, residence, washing, and uniform, subject to the provisions of the Superannuation Act. Par- ticulars of the duties may be obtained from the Master. Applications, stating age, experience (if any), with copies of two testimonials of recent date, to reach my Office not later than Tuesday morn- ing next, the 26th January, 1915. W. E. HOUGH, Acting Clerk to the Guardians. Union Offices, 71, High-street, Runcorn.</p>
        <p>• COUNTY BOROUCiII OF WARRINGTON. The Sanitary Works Committee are pre- pared to receive TENDERS for the supply of the following Materials for Longford Depot for a period of twelve months, commencing Ist April next:— WROUGHT IRON, BOLTS, CASTINGS, TOOLS, OILS, PACKING, BRICKS, VITRIOL, &amp;c.; also for CARTING. Samples of goods required may be seen and specification and form of tender may be obtained from the undersigned. Tenders, securely fastened, must be addressed "The Chairman, Sanitary Works Committee, Town Hall, Warrington, endorsed "Tender for Depot Materials,' and delivered not later than 10 a.m. on Tuesday, 2nd February, 1915. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily he accepted. R. WILSON, Manager. Longford Depot, Warrington, 20th January, 1915.</p>
