        <p>ALTRINCHAM .AMATEUR CUP. STOCKTON HEATH'S FORTHCOMING FIXTURE WITH CADISHEAD WESLEYANS The meeting of the above clubs in the Altrinc- ham Amateur Cup Competition is being looked forward to with much confidence in the camp of the • "Heathens" supporters. The two clubs have met twice during the prpsent season in the North Cheshire League Competition, and both games have resulted in an equal division of the points. Th'e "Heathens" are the only team who have extracted two points from the Wes- leyans, and as in to-day's struggle • they have the choice of ground,- their chances of victory appear to be very rosy. The following players have been selected to represent the Stockton Heath Club : Eloper; Gosling and Cheaters; Rylance, Bar- low and West; Lloyd, Noden, Vernon, Smith and Pearse. The referee will be Mr. H. Smith, of Latch- ford. Unfortunately for the "Heathens," Bates ill not be able to resume his position at centre- forward owing to injuries, and Starkey will also be absent, •having joined Kitchener's Army.</p>
